WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.748
Step 1. Open the encounter Overview.

1.2
00:00:02.748 --> 00:00:08.506
You see a patient's procedures in two places: the Procedures panel of an encounter,

1.3
00:00:08.506 --> 00:00:12.753
and Past Procedures in the patient's clinical history.

2.1
00:00:12.753 --> 00:00:15.370
Step 2. Find the Procedures panel.

2.2
00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:20.733
The panel shows only when the encounter has a procedure that is not marked as

2.3
00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:22.416
entered in error.

3.1
00:00:22.416 --> 00:00:25.611
Step 3. Read the procedures in the panel.

3.2
00:00:25.611 --> 00:00:31.142
Each row shows the procedure, its status, its outcome and the date performed,

3.3
00:00:31.142 --> 00:00:34.587
with the newest recorded procedure first.

4.1
00:00:34.587 --> 00:00:37.615
Step 4. Read the note of a procedure.

4.2
00:00:37.615 --> 00:00:41.668
Select the info icon on the row, then select See Note.

4.3
00:00:41.668 --> 00:00:46.672
A green dot on the icon shows that the procedure has a note.

5.1
00:00:46.672 --> 00:00:51.781
Step 5. Open Past Procedures. Select the History link on the panel.

5.2
00:00:51.781 --> 00:00:57.285
Care opens the patient's clinical history on the Past Procedures tab.

6.1
00:00:57.285 --> 00:00:59.632
Step 6. Read Past Procedures.

6.2
00:00:59.632 --> 00:01:04.403
This tab lists the procedures from every encounter of the patient,

6.3
00:01:04.403 --> 00:01:10.615
grouped by the day each one was recorded in Care, not the day it was performed.

7.1
00:01:10.615 --> 00:01:17.980
Step 7. Leave Past Procedures. Select Back to Encounter to return to the encounter.
